00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.869 align:start position:0%
 
oops  hi I'm Samir and I made a mostly silent  song that made the top 30 on the iTunes  charts so it was a Sunday morning I'm  sitting at Starbucks  I'm think to myself gosh you know what I  hate I hate that every time I plug my  phone into my car the song from Taylor  Swift all you had to do was stay plays  for a lot of people it's Kendrick  Lamar's ADHD or Ed Sheeran's a team or  even Vampire Weekend's a punk there are  a lot more I think those were some of  the more simple ones that they came  across the reason it plays is the way  iPhones are set up is that it plays the  first song alphabetically into your car  so I tell myself I got to do something  about this I can't do this anymore I'm  gonna make a blank song that plays to  give me enough time to go figure out  whatever song that I want to play so I  knew this was a problem because years  before I wrote a BuzzFeed post about it  because at that time a punk by Vampire  Weekend was doing that to me  and I even asked them to change the name  of the song but obviously they didn't do  that so it occurred to me that I gotta  do something about this enough is enough  and I happen to have my laptop have my  phone I'm like I'm gonna do this right  now  I started looking into how do you get  songs into iTunes how does that work so  I figured it out I learned that the way  music it's on to iTunes Spotify Google  Play Store all these places is through a  music distributor so I looked around  found one that seemed to make sense  seemed to be legit seemed to be the one  that people liked so then after that I  looked around to find some mp3 software  I figured I would make it about 20  minutes I recorded the track and then  just through the music software I just  deleted the audio off of it  so I named the song a space a space a  space a very good song first thing that  came to mind I think it was five days  this covered like pretty much most  people's problem and then I named the  album have a wonderful day because I  assumed people would plug their phone in  and see this often so I just wanted to  make it kind of happy it took a few days  to earn it all out figure it out and  then by Wednesday I uploaded it out to  the services and I wanted to charge like  a little bit of money for at $0.99  seemed like that's not crazy for it but  I learned  when you uploaded that long it requires  the person to buy an album $9.99 and of  course that's ridiculous so then I  figured out it needs to be under ten  minutes so I cut it down which if you  actually listen to the whole thing  you'll notice that I say something right  at the very end telling you to change  the track but I think I say it's been 26  minutes and then it's good for you to  change the track I thought I had  uploaded the right version but I guess I  didn't so then I uploaded it to iTunes I  tweeted it out and I was quickly picked  up by one of my friends at fader from  there they've just kind of totally blew  up so many places wrote about it  Lifehacker Mashable realest Popular  Mechanics AV Club BuzzFeed frosted  reviews wired Apple Insider W genius  Cosmo variety NPR today talked about  this new song that is climbing the  charts on iTunes and the reason behind  it it's a little bit unusual people are  buying the silent song that was created  to be the first song to play when you  plug your phone into your car so it's  just kind of like steam rolling from  there and then I went out to dinner and  then Twitter picked it up as a moment  and that's when it just kind of went  like crazy viral so many people quote  tweeting saying you're genius I love  this song is what I've always needed  tagging their friends that have the  problem saying the songs whatever that  they had a problem with it was just like  so crazy it was so much fun next morning  I wake up I think my brother or someone  texted me and told me that your song is  on the iTunes charts I think it got as  high as number 30 so like all day that  next day it's just kind of like going up  and down the charts sometimes later that  day I get a random text from my cousin  and he says you're trending on iTunes  and I went to iTunes and my name was at  the top of that trend Inglis  so while this is happening all these  crazy things are going through my head  and I got a little platinum do I get to  go to the MTV Music Awards radio  stations reached out I did something on  Fox and I thought oh my gosh I'm rich I  could retire life is over but I quickly  realized that that wasn't the case there  seems to be a huge exponential kind of  drop-off and how like the top artists  make money on there and how they not top  ten or whatever seem to make money so  yeah I'm still working it was it wasn't  that much it felt really good it looks  felt really cool to be viral like random  people that I know or see around that I  don't really ever talk to you would be  like hey I saw you on TV I saw your song  random text messages from friends old  family Facebook friends that I don't  really talk to that would tag me in  their post saying my friends Samir  created this song I'd worked at BuzzFeed  before I'd been a part of so many things  going viral but it had never been like  me that was the topic so it was pretty  fun to like to be in the spotlight I  want to say like the full viral in this  craze probably lasted about a week as  far as next steps  maybe there's a music video coming out  yeah I don't know I hope I'm not a  one-hit wonder but we'll see if I don't  know if I come up with something else  would it just be like a black screen I  was thinking of like driving around I  don't know there's so many different  ways that I could maybe shoot a music  video for it  yeah perfect that's got real quick  [Music]

